{"schemaVersion":"boolean-creep-review/v1","id":"r2-apps-vault-sync-command-busy","sourceSha":"5f1a88ddaa215372e528b2f900207f0663644a25","reviewer":"grok-cli","evidenceStatus":"pass","designStatus":"finding","findings":[{"area":"design","severity":"blocking","note":"Migration inventory deletes the connected local at VaultSyncPanel.tsx:306-308 and says to inline status.value.connected once at the trigger disabled expression, but ConnectionBadge at :325 still reads that local as a boolean prop. vault-sync-status-connected later owns the badge union migration and still assumes the boolean prop until then; deleting the local as written is a compile break or a second unnamed inline the design forbids."}]}
{"schemaVersion":"boolean-creep-review/v1","id":"r2-tooling-packet-transition-stream-trace","sourceSha":"5f1a88ddaa215372e528b2f900207f0663644a25","reviewer":"grok-cli","evidenceStatus":"pass","designStatus":"finding","findings":[{"area":"design","severity":"blocking","note":"SetStatus.ts:419 reads outcome.disposition === \"skipped\" after commit and otherwise logs an append. The design splits outcome disposition into skipped-fresh|skipped-refreshed|appended|streamless and claims SetStatus consumes plan types only. Following that list leaves the skipped CLI arm dead, so skipped-fresh/skipped-refreshed commits print the append message. Plan disposition at SetStatus.ts:270 stays skipped and is not this reader."}]}
